# Line endings.
#
# This checkout runs with core.autocrlf=true, so without a rule here git hands
# every text file to the working tree with CRLF. For sources that is harmless.
# For the shell scripts it is not: they are run by WSL bash, and a `\r` on the
# shebang line makes the kernel pick /bin/sh instead of bash, so the script
# fails with "set: pipefail: invalid option name" followed by a syntax error at
# end of file -- a failure that names neither the cause nor the file's encoding.
#
# `scripts/device_compile_kernels.sh` is the project's BiSheng dav-3510 compile
# gate (CLAUDE.md section 5.1) and `scripts/verify_npu_build.sh` is the NPU
# build gate (section 5.3). Both are documented to be invoked as
# `wsl -d Ubuntu-22.04 -- bash /mnt/c/ascend-moe-engine/scripts/<name>.sh`, so
# they have to survive a Windows checkout with LF intact.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf
configure text eol=lf

# CMake drives those same scripts and is read by WSL tooling as well.
*.cmake        text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf

# Simulator and driver output that is regenerated on every camodel run; see the
# .gitignore entries for why none of it is tracked.
*.dump binary
*.bin  binary
